Since April, people have reported bookings landing on the wrong day. The desk merged overlapping export rows into #4471.

The report IDs must be deduplicated before counting. The cause follows the tenant locale, booking form, and channel—not the intake tag, which is only a guess.

Separate issues track the day-first parser failure and the booking-v3 date-hint failure: [parser issue](https://github.com/pmatysek/MEGA.dev.s01e03/issues/1) and [form-hint issue](https://github.com/pmatysek/MEGA.dev.s01e03/issues/2).

<Callout>
Parser fixed. The booking-v3 form-hint issue will not be fixed because that form has been retired.
</Callout>

## Causes and coverage

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## Engineering update

- Parser: fixed with `fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales` (issue #1).
- Hint: not planned because the booking-v3 form was retired (issue #2).

## Queue history

<QueueTimeline ticket={4471} />

## Triage notes

- The parser cause covers dates interpreted month-first for day-first tenants.
- The form-hint cause covers booking-v3 form reports where the MM/DD/YYYY hint conflicts with the day-first locale.
- A one-day move is not automatically a timezone issue; the desk's noted reports remain filed by tenant cause.

